#Armor Type
; Fleet capitals retain 10% capital-beam damage. Command stations take 25%
; capital-beam damage and additionally resist light weapons and debris impacts.
; Station hull/scaling lives in fs2rts_config.lua, not the old 132,600 HP sweeps.
$Name: RTS Base Hull
$Damage Type: RTS Capital Beam
+Calculation: multiplicative
+Value: 0.10
$Damage Type: RTS Static Artillery
+Calculation: multiplicative
+Value: 0.10
$Name: RTS Command Hull
$Damage Type: RTS Capital Beam
+Calculation: multiplicative
+Value: 0.25
$Damage Type: RTS Static Artillery
; Cheap 11 km sentries defend approaches; mobile siege must finish a station.
+Calculation: multiplicative
+Value: 0.025
$Damage Type: RTS Light Weapons
+Calculation: multiplicative
+Value: 0.05
$Damage Type: RTS Fighter Weapons
+Calculation: multiplicative
+Value: 0.05
$Damage Type: RTS Debris Impact
; An upstream rush replay lost 53k hull to one wreckage impact. Keep small
; impacts intact, but cap any one piece at <0.5% of a normal command station.
+Calculation: cap
+Value: 250
; Subsystems share this armor. Avoid applying the nearest subsystem's armor
; to the hull as well: native hull/subsystem paths each apply it once.
$Flags: ("ignore subsystem armor")
#End
